hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1794","Narrated Haritha bin Wahb Khuzai (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Shall I not inform you about the people of Paradise (who they are)? Every weak and humble person whom people consider insignificant, but if he swears by Allah about something, Allah fulfills it for him. And shall I not inform you about the people of Hell (who they are)? The people of Hell are the wicked, arrogant, and proud ones."
"1795","´Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “(On the Day of Resurrection) our Lord will uncover His shin, and all believing men and women will prostrate. But those who used to pray in the world to show off to people and to be heard by them, they will also try to prostrate, but their backs will become stiff like a board (they will not be able to bend and will not be able to prostrate).”"
